        "original_id": "9cc378a7-d1c5-5908-8682-b297e2a3f3c3",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: William Bainbridge, John Adams, Abigail Adams\n- Organizations: United States Navy, Royal Navy\n- Products: USS Bainbridge (DDG-96), USS Constitution, HMS Java\n- Events: War of 1812\n- Roles: Commodore, President\n\nFacts:\n- William Bainbridge was born on May 7, 1774, and died on July 27, 1833.\n- William Bainbridge was a Commodore in the United States Navy.\n- During his long career in the early United States Navy, William Bainbridge served under six presidents beginning with President John Adams.\n- John Adams was a dedicated diarist and correspondent, especially with his wife and closest advisor, Abigail Adams.\n- In the War of 1812, Commodore William Bainbridge commanded USS Constitution when it and its crew captured HMS Java, a 38-gun fifth-rate frigate of the Royal Navy.\n- USS Bainbridge (DDG-96) is named in honor of Commodore William Bainbridge.\n- William Bainbridge is notable for his many victories at sea.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "dcec3131-354e-5972-959d-09359994e289",
        "text": "Page: William Bainbridge. Sentence: William Bainbridge (May 7, 1774 – July 27, 1833) was a Commodore in the United States Navy.\nPage: William Bainbridge. Sentence: During his long career in the young American Navy he served under six presidents beginning with John Adams and is notable for his many victories at sea.\nPage: John Adams. Sentence: He was also a dedicated diarist and correspondent, particularly with his wife and closest advisor Abigail.\nPage: USS Bainbridge (DDG-96). Sentence: \"Bainbridge\" is named in honor of Commodore William Bainbridge, who as commander of the frigate USS \"Constitution\" distinguished himself in the War of 1812 when he and his crew captured HMS \"Java\", a 38-gun fifth-rate frigate of the Royal Navy.",
